{"text":"out. The order is stable from one read to the next while nothing new is loaded, but it isn’t one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you choose. Sort the values when order matters:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let migrations = LinkerSet<Migration>(kind: .migrations).values.sorted { $0.version < $1.version }"]},{"text":"When records are read","type":"heading","anchor":"When-records-are-read","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing runs at launch. Each read of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet\/records","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" asks the loader for its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"images and walks their records, so a read after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"type":"text","text":" includes the new library’s records. A read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"walks every record of every kind, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in their number; keep the result rather than reading it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a hot loop."}]},{"text":"Records one at a time","type":"heading","anchor":"Records-one-at-a-time","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet\/records"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the records themselves, of the set’s kind, before any type is asked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetRecord\/value(as:)"},{"type":"text","text":" asks one record for a value and says why it can’t produce one:"}]},{"type":"codeListin